Unfortunately due to instability of NAO, it was a local game, so my stats
won't reflect that if you search NAO:

Quick Walk through - Early Game
================================

Started out as a wizard-human-male-neutral. Got quickly up to XL 5 or 6
and then tackled Gnomish mines. I was still using standard weapon (blessed
quarterstaff) and AC was poor. I picked up +1 leather armor and +0 leather
gloves.

Made use of food to have tame pets (dogs and cats) and entered the
Minetown. Luckily, the altar was aligned - neutral, with aligned Priest
sitting there. Also there was a rare book store in Minetown, and using
tame pet I managed to acquire most of the '+' books (about 6) and only
paid for 1 book. My pet took the rest. Good boy!

Useful spells of fireball, identify and magic missile were gained,
although my casting was still 'basic' for attack. I managed to use Force
Bolt to get skilled pretty quickly, so fireball was MUCH more effective.

I managed to goto the Mines End, and get 2 Gray Stones which I knew
weren't a loadstone (I always kick them first!). Managed to identify a
luckstone and flint stone. Discarded the flintstone and took some
(unidentified) gems back up too.

I made use of my 2 magic markers I'd pick up, by #dipping potions and
scrolls in { fountains to blank them. Using an aligned altar on level5 and
Minetown, I made holy water and wrote enchant armor scrolls and dipped
them to get blessed. My AC was around -5 or -6 at this point. I managed to
identify some real gems, rubies;emeralds etc, and maxed out my luck by
throwing them at a gray unicorn in the mines. When I #dipped at Delphi to
blank a scrolls I got a demon released who granted my a wish! Got a
blessed fixed +2 silver dragon scale mail which is a standard 1st wish as
a wizard. This gave me reflection and I was still wearing a blessed +3
cloak of MR. My AC was around -13 at this point.

I then did sokoban, only to find another "oReflection and not a bag of
holding as I hoped. I also had a ring of slow digestion on (started with
this), and found another.

Finishing the Quest - The Dark One...
=====================================

Around level 13, I found another aligned temple. Stated to make my stash
here. Dropped many spellbooks, rings and wands.

With my luck maxed out, I prayed at Minetown altar and manged to get
rustproof Magicbane. Use blessed scroll of enchant weapon to get it to +2.
Headed back up...

Level 14, I found magic portal in vault and got to Fort Ludios. A bit
tedious but I cleared out whole of the Fort. Using Fireball and Cone of
Cold spells frequently. I had reflection which was essential, but luckily
there was no Black Dragon and its disintegration attacks.

From the Fort I managed to get 40k in gold and managed to get to XL 14
(enchanter) for the quest. Headed back to priest on L13 and used the gold
for 'the protection racket' and naked, took my AC down from 10 to 1. My AC
was around -19 at this point. I also used a wand of enlightenment (15
charges!) to quickly find out when I could pray, without my usual 'create
monster' wand or spell and #offer at the altar. Using this, with my luck
('extremely luck' and 'extra luck'), I managed to be crowned, "Envoy of
Balance" and got all intrinsic (fire,cold,sleep,shock and poison
resistance).

I also ate a 'Q' (Quantum Mechanic) so I was fast, and I was wearing
blessed +3 speed boots, thus 'very fast' - which helps a lot.

Completed the Dark One easily - At last level of Quest I managed to get a
Wand of Wishing with three charges in it too! Blessed scrolls of charging,
plus ring of levitation and conflict, and still had some charges in my
/WoW left..which was essential for Astral Planes! Read on!


Late Game - Wizard and First Encounter with Demigorgon
======================================================

Medusa was easy. I fell in trap door and went below Medusa level. I've got
killed before by climbing up and not being blind - turned to stone
instantly - so I quaffed a cursed potion blindness and went up stairs. She
died instantly without a fight.

Cleared out the castle - using levitation I went round the rear as I
always hate the drawbridge. By this time I'd read 3 blessed scrolls of
genocide. My rules for genociding races are, (1) 'h' to get rid of all
mind flayers, (2) 'L' get rid of all types of Liches. The 3rd one was to
get rid of all 'D' for dragons and disenchanters. Maybe it's a waste.
Later in the game I read 4th blessed scroll and got rid of all 'H' for all
types of giants and minotaurs.

The castle was great fun - using fireball and cone of cold from a
distance. By this point my AC was -25, and just waded in with +2 Magicbane
for the sheer hell (and joy) of it. I was enjoying myself a lot here.
Picked up the usual /WoW - only had 1 charge (boo!) and wished for 2
blessed scrolls of charging. Re-charged the WoW and wished for blessed +2
robe, which helps spellcasting a lot. Since I had MR from artifact and
Magicbane, I ditched cloak of MR. My AC was -26, HP only around 120, but
magic was around 200.

I only had a uncursed sack, not holding - I never wished for one, so I
returned to level 14 where I stashed my spellbooks at this point in order
to refresh my memory - the spells wear out after 20k turns.

Valley of Dead was straight forward - no major problems. Got a spellbook
of dig here. I managed to bribe Asmodeus and Baalzebub - they went away. 
Orcus did not oblige, but luckily I anticipated this by not killing a
chickatrice in the shops nearby. I used sleep spell on him whilst I
cleared out the rest of the level. Then killed the 'c' and it left a
corpse (luckily). Wielded the chickatrice corpse and stoned Orcus and
Vampire Lord in the same room. Used pick-axe to shatter the Orcus statue
and got a wand of dead and a large amount of satisfaction!

Jubilex engulfed me as normal and I was 'ill' then 'very ill'. Managed to
kill him and (a)pply blessed unicorn horn - What a relief!

I had 2 blessed amulets of life saving at this point, so I worn one and
bagged one. I was wearing ring of slow digestion most of the time.

level 34 - found Vlad's tower. Killed Vlad and got candelabrum and another
Amulet of LS. Used magic mapping spell to get to level47 and located
vibrating square. Use my pick axe to ensure all Gehennom levels had quick
routes between '<' and '>'.

Went to level 46 and Wizards tower. Wizard summoned monsters and stole my
artifact. Here I died for 1st time, put on 2nd Amulet of LS. Killed wizard
with cone of cold. Got the book of the dead and my artifact back and
managed to get to Moloch's Sanctum by the usual ritual at the vibrating
square.

On entering the sanctum I was met by '&' Yeenoghu. He then proceeded to
summon '&' Demigorgon. I was scared. Killed Yeenoghu but the demigorgon
had made me ill and I was taking serious damage. Used my rapidly declining
WoW to get 'blessed cockatrice corpse' and killed the demigorgon by
stoning. Using pick-axe I shattered the statue to find the real Amulet of
Yendor and another Amulet of Life Saving. So I never had to get the
Sanctum and kill the Priest after all. I did a #name for the "oY and it
wouldn't go into my sack - so it was real enough. Headed back up,
annoyingly getting transported back down a few times, but luckily did not
meet the wizard. Got back to my stash at level14, and was met by Archon -
thanks. Killed him - he left a long sword named Demonbane. I really should
have taken it, but I left for the endgame with no more wizard or Archon
appearances.

Endgame and the Astral Plane Dilemma
=====================================

Plane of Earth was ok, wizard appears straight away and used my cone of
cold at close range to kill him. He appeared twice on this level but
luckily did not summon.

Plane of Air. Really tough level. Those air elementals are tough for HP of
161 and +2 Magicbane. Use /oDeath several times. Even though, I got killed
2nd time, and put on another Amulet of LS. I was wearing levitation and
conflict rings here. Saw 'ki-rin' and he was summoning nasties all the
time. Used /oDeath. Then got another Archon and was using teleport away
spell to ensure I didn't die again.  I had to use my LAST official WoW
charge for another blessed cockatrice corpse to get rid of Archon. 
Luckily I got to magic portal, and if I stayed much longer I don't think I
would have survived much more.

Plane of Fire. Due to fire resistance, elementals are easier. Wizard
showed up again and killed him with cone of cold spells. Then another
Archon showed up - used a couple of teleport away spells and wished I had
more wands of teleportation as these spells were expensive with the
"oYendor in tow. Again I was beginning to panic when I managed to stumble
on the magic portal. Need a quick way of locating that portal for future
reference. ?oGD maybe. I didn't have any of them anyway.

Plane of Water. Running low on food, so I used ring of conflict and slow
digestion and stayed within the bubbles. Wizard showed up again and stole
the "oYendor. I killed him again with cone of cold attacks, but panicked
when he died and I couldn't find the Amulet. Luckily I managed to stay
within the bubbles and eventually found his corpse with the Amulet.

Astral Plane
============

Got a tame Angel and headed left for the 1st temple. Famine showed up and
used wand of lightening for a kill. Put my ring of conflict on (I'd taken
it off before coming here), and all hell kicked off. I was taking a
serious beating and using teleport away managed to get to the 1st Sanctum.
Jump spells weren't working - the priests always seemed to be in the way.
I was low on HP and Pwr and getting to the 1st Sanctum I used my last
"oLS. I wasn't going to make it to the 2nd or 3rd altar. I was NEUTRAL, so
I hoped it was too.

It wasn't. It was Chaotic altar. I was in deep trouble and it looked like
I was about to die on the Astral Plane.

I decided my only option was to change alignments and ascend at this
altar. Therefore I needed a 'Helm of Opposite Alignment' and I did not
have one. I only had a 'wand of wishing (1:0)' and I would need to zap it
many times to get a wish out of the worn out wand.

I decided to clear out the temple and lock the door. The priest was still
summoning insects and I had to step on the door as another priest had died
there and left stuff. The door would not close. Managed to pick up all the
stuff, step back, drop the priest robe and shield etc. Then I got
lucky...summon monster again and a 't' trapper was on the other side of
the door - lock the door and none of the Angels or Priests outside could
get to me.

Frantically zapped the dud WoW. 'Nothing happens'...Then finally, got,
"You wrest one last charge from the worn-out wand.  You may wish for an
object". Wished for 'Blessed +2 Helm of Opposite Alignment". Put it
on....it was a cursed -3 HoA..and I was LAWFUL, not chaotic. My remove
curse spell had expired and I didn't have that spellbook with me. Had
blank paper and about 13 charges left in my Magic Marker. Wrote a remove
curse scroll, and took off Helm. Wore it again. I as lawful again. I had
no more ?oRC left or methods to make one. Luckily I had 4 !holy water in
my sack. Took them out. #dip Helm in !holy water. Took off - Wore it. I
was still LAWFUL! Repeated this and I was CHAOTIC.

Approached the alter and #offer the "oY...

"An invisible choir sings, and you are bathed in radiance"

....My first Ascension was done... What a relief!!!

